# Developer Ownership

The following decisions belong to the developer and should **never** be overridden or second-guessed unless explicitly asked.

## Data Interpretation
- Which numbers to highlight or feature prominently
- How to frame trends and what they mean in context
- What narrative angle to take on the data

## Narrative & Language
- Section titles, chart titles, and axis labels
- Any written commentary or introductory text accompanying visualisations
- Any bilingual or localised UI strings — the developer owns these

## Design Decisions
- Colour palette and visual hierarchy
- Layout and section ordering
- What to emphasise visually

## Default Stack Preferences
Unless a project specifies otherwise, assume this preferred stack:

- **Backend:** FastAPI (not Flask, Django, or any other framework)
- **Frontend:** HTMX + Tailwind CSS (not React, Vue, or Alpine.js)
- **Charts:** ECharts v5 (not Chart.js, D3, Recharts, or Plotly)
- **Templates:** Jinja2

Do not suggest alternatives to these unless a hard technical blocker is encountered.
